Put $u=x-10$, $v=y-5$; this translation does not change areas, and the region becomes $|u|+|v|\le100$. In each quadrant this is a right triangle with legs $100$, for instance $u,v\ge0$, $u+v\le100$. So the region is a square (a ``diamond'') centred at $(10,5)$ with vertices $(110,5)$, $(10,105)$, $(-90,5)$, $(10,-95)$.

\begin{asy}
